OL,3,GNEWSACouncil proposes 20mph speed
OL,4,Alimits near schools
OL,5,
OL,6,FNew 20mph (32km/h) speed limits could
OL,7,Fbe introduced around schools in a bid
OL,8,Fto make it safer for pupils.
OL,10,FTorbay Council said zones could be
OL,11,Finstalled near six schools in Torquay,
OL,12,FPaignton and Brixham on and near roads
OL,13,Fwith a "high level of pedestrian to
OL,14,Fvehicle conflict".
OL,16,FIt said 20mph limits had been proposed
OL,17,Ffor residential roads with a "high
OL,18,Fvolume of use by school children" and
OL,19,Fin urban areas to help "reduce
OL,20,Faccidents, cut noise, improve air
OL,21,Fquality and give drivers more time to
OL,22,Freact".
OL,23,APub: 03-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
